    {
      "id": "claim_d512433d8b114757b964025df55ab19f",
      "statement": "`scripts/ci.sh` is the provider-agnostic single source of truth for renderer CI, running from the repo root under `set -euo pipefail` in order: install (`npm ci` or `npm install`, skippable via `SKIP_INSTALL=1`), typecheck (`npm run typecheck`), wiki-link check (`npm run check:wiki`), unit tests (`npm test`), integration tests (`npm run test:integration`), and the static SPA build (`npm run build`).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/ci.sh#L1-L53",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:71b62054b373cb9fdd44f8c3c94d903896dff57ec10d004d83c4f887f25fbc9a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_51fff641705d42c6874e4ee2297d91eb",
      "statement": "`.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs `scripts/ci.sh` on `ubuntu-latest` (Node 24) on push to `main` and `release/**` and on every pull request, with `paths-ignore: technical-report/**`; it deliberately adds no push-on-every-branch trigger (a PR branch would build twice) and uses a concurrency group `${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}` with `cancel-in-progress: true`.",
