    {
      "id": "claim_9c27d5e47c364529828874b8c72e96a0",
      "statement": "`openwiki.yml` is the scheduled weekly (Monday 06:00 UTC) OpenWiki refresh, but it does no work inline: it is a thin reusable-workflow call that delegates entirely to `ardoco/actions/.github/workflows/openwiki.yml@main` (triggered via `workflow_dispatch` + cron), passing the `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` secret. The actual generation logic — installing the `openwiki` CLI, running `--update --print`, opening a PR — lives in that shared workflow, not in this repo's file.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/openwiki.yml#L1-L17",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bf077ccef0e2cd34134360b05d6efa4f00b44ee578eb40b00f56b6ed10ae9927:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4935551a39d0407ea70e00c43c21c122",
      "statement": "`wiki-publish.yml` triggers on push to `main` under `openwiki/**`, `user-guide/**`, `.github/wiki-assets/**`, or the workflow file (plus `workflow_dispatch`), and replaces the GitHub wiki with a combined layout: `Home.md` (always `.github/wiki-assets/Home.md` verbatim), `Development.md` (from `openwiki/Home.md`, renamed), the rest of `openwiki/*.md` flat at the wiki root, `openwiki/{concepts,operations,workflows}/*.md` flattened under explicit `Section-Page` names, flattened `user-guide/*.md` renamed to `Guide-*`, `user-guide/screenshots/**` flattened alongside, and a global `_Sidebar.md`/`_Footer.md` assembled from `.github/wiki-assets/` plus a user-guide fragment wrapped in `<!-- wiki-sync:NAME:start/end -->` marker pairs. It strips OKF frontmatter, rewrites cross-links for extensionless wiki URLs (including `Home`→`Development` in the sidebar and `../README.md`→absolute GitHub URLs in the user guide), `rsync --delete` replaces the wiki, and commits as `github-actions[bot]` with a `[wiki-sync]` marker. `index.md` and `INSTRUCTIONS.md` are deliberately excluded.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/wiki-publish.yml#L1-L358",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f02c26fba34372574b4eff10920709c141c3c102079ecab15f3cf145ab2b50cb:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_66c08000247f4650aee1ec43741d1cea",
      "statement": "`wiki-import.yml` is the reverse direction, triggering on `gollum` (wiki create/update) and `workflow_dispatch`; it shares a `concurrency: group: wiki-sync` with `wiki-publish.yml`, and its sender guard skips `github-actions[bot]` (unless `workflow_dispatch`). It clones the wiki and maps each published piece back to its repo source: `Home.md` is dropped if it still carries the `<!-- wiki-sync:auto-home -->` marker, otherwise replaces `.github/wiki-assets/Home.md`; `Development.md`→`openwiki/Home.md`; the `Section-Page` flattened pages→`openwiki/{section}/<page>.md` (reversing the name flattening and cross-link rewrites); flattened `Guide-*`→`user-guide/<src>.md` (reversing renames, link rewrites, and absolute URLs back to `../README.md`/`../LICENSE`); `screenshots/`→`user-guide/screenshots/`; the `_Sidebar`/`_Footer` user-guide fragments→`.github/wiki-assets/` (lifted out of their `<!-- wiki-sync:NAME:start/end -->` marker pairs) with the `Development`→`Home` link reversed; then `rsync --delete --include '*.md' --exclude '*'` mirrors remaining `*.md` into `openwiki/` and commits to `main` with a `[wiki-sync]` marker.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/wiki-import.yml#L1-L255",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ba83bbd0d4a86079df095c2fce173d261f739b7b9aab81d0efec08bd65e04f2c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b09ea28534f1489798a30923839c0643",
      "statement": "Publish and import would otherwise form an infinite loop (publish→gollum→import→main push→publish). Three independent layers prevent it: both share a `concurrency: group: wiki-sync` with `cancel-in-progress: false` so they never run concurrently; `wiki-publish.yml` skips commits whose message contains `[wiki-sync]`; and `wiki-import.yml` skips when `github.event.sender.login == 'github-actions[bot]'`, so each direction only reacts to human-originated changes on the other side.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/wiki-import.yml#L24-L35",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ab79fdb3ae7adddda86fece738cfc584219502441c27d7d38b795885c9317f7c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/wiki-publish.yml#L75-L87",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:98fb6dbf70932bb04d9b39f53c61ab924d7f85f863f12d682ad043418a3fcd3c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_428e341a9def4907b761ad8abec10169",
      "statement": "The desktop build is `npx tauri build`: `tauri.conf.json` reads the version from `../package.json`, rebuilds the renderer via `beforeBuildCommand: npm run build` into `frontendDist: ../dist`, bundles with `targets: \"all\"` and macOS minimum system version 15.0, and points the updater plugin at the `latest.json` release-download endpoint with `requireSignedVersion: true` and an embedded pubkey.",
      "evidence": [
